{"content_hash": "8093de8e0b6ae9dd", "version_id": 462, "article_id": 47, "level_code": "en_a2", "lang": "en", "level": 2, "level_label": "A2 初级", "title": "Flock cuts 270 jobs as cities turn against its cameras", "title_zh": "Flock 要裁 270 人，各地开始反对它的摄像头", "has_translation": true, "topic": "tech", "source": "guardian_tech", "source_url": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/09/flock-job-cuts", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1562739974-e15519c03d87?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8OHx8c3VydmVpbGxhbmNlJTIwc3RhcnR1cCUyMGZsb2NrfGVufDB8MHx8fDE3OTE2NjU4NTR8MA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Kaspars Eglitis on Unsplash", "author": "Kaspars Eglitis", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@kasparseglitis?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/bird-on-white-cctv-camera-BCMCMuTISio?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(321, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(359, 46%, 48%)", "label": "TECH", "seed": "9651cefffeca"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-09", "word_count": 121, "reading_minutes": 0.6, "lead": "Flock makes AI cameras that read car license plates. Now many people and lawmakers say no to them. The company is cutting jobs.", "lead_zh": "Flock 生产能识别车牌的 AI 摄像头。现在很多人和议员都表示反对。公司正在裁员。", "preview": "Flock Safety will cut about 270 jobs, or 18% of its workers. The staff will leave at the end of the month. The company has about 1,500 emplo", "preview_zh": "Flock Safety 将裁掉约 270 个岗位，占员工总数的 18%。这些员工将在月底离开。公司约有 1500 名员工，不愿对此置评。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 455, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/47/en_a2.mp3", "duration": 57.288, "size_bytes": 347472, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural", "word_count": 144, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@fc48a26/content/data/versions/462.json", "paragraphs": ["Flock Safety will cut about 270 jobs, or 18% of its workers. The staff will leave at the end of the month. The company has about 1,500 employees and did not want to talk about it.", "Flock is based in Atlanta and started in 2017. It has about 120,000 cameras in 49 states. The cameras read license plates on streets and highways. Police and businesses use them.", "But many people worry about privacy. A new poll shows 38% of Americans like the cameras, and 47% do not. In September, Florida banned these cameras from state highways.", "Flock also faces a lawsuit in Virginia. Investors at Home Depot want checks on such partners. The company raised over $950m and is worth $7.5bn."], "paragraphs_zh": ["Flock Safety 将裁掉约 270 个岗位，占员工总数的 18%。这些员工将在月底离开。公司约有 1500 名员工，不愿对此置评。", "Flock 总部在亚特兰大，2017 年成立。它在 49 个州装了约 12 万个摄像头。这些摄像头在街道和高速公路上识别车牌。警察和企业都在使用。", "但很多人担心隐私问题。一项新调查显示，38% 的美国人喜欢这些摄像头，47% 的人不喜欢。9 月，佛罗里达州禁止在州高速公路上使用这类摄像头。", "Flock 在弗吉尼亚州还面临一起诉讼。家得宝的投资者希望审查这类合作伙伴。公司已融资超过 9.5 亿美元，估值 75 亿美元。"], "body": "Flock Safety will cut about 270 jobs, or 18% of its workers. The staff will leave at the end of the month. The company has about 1,500 employees and did not want to talk about it.\n\nFlock is based in Atlanta and started in 2017. It has about 120,000 cameras in 49 states. The cameras read license plates on streets and highways. Police and businesses use them.\n\nBut many people worry about privacy. A new poll shows 38% of Americans like the cameras, and 47% do not. In September, Florida banned these cameras from state highways.\n\nFlock also faces a lawsuit in Virginia. Investors at Home Depot want checks on such partners. The company raised over $950m and is worth $7.5bn.", "body_zh": "Flock Safety 将裁掉约 270 个岗位，占员工总数的 18%。这些员工将在月底离开。公司约有 1500 名员工，不愿对此置评。\n\nFlock 总部在亚特兰大，2017 年成立。它在 49 个州装了约 12 万个摄像头。这些摄像头在街道和高速公路上识别车牌。警察和企业都在使用。\n\n但很多人担心隐私问题。一项新调查显示，38% 的美国人喜欢这些摄像头，47% 的人不喜欢。9 月，佛罗里达州禁止在州高速公路上使用这类摄像头。\n\nFlock 在弗吉尼亚州还面临一起诉讼。家得宝的投资者希望审查这类合作伙伴。公司已融资超过 9.5 亿美元，估值 75 亿美元。", "text": "Flock Safety will cut about 270 jobs, or 18% of its workers. The staff will leave at the end of the month. The company has about 1,500 employees and did not want to talk about it. Flock is based in Atlanta and started in 2017. It has about 120,000 cameras in 49 states. The cameras read license plates on streets and highways. Police and businesses use them. But many people worry about privacy. A new poll shows 38% of Americans like the cameras, and 47% do not. In September, Florida banned these cameras from state highways. Flock also faces a lawsuit in Virginia. Investors at Home Depot want checks on such partners. The company raised over $950m and is worth $7.5bn.", "vocab": [{"word": "cut jobs", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "裁员", "note": "也可以说 cut positions", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "employee", "pos": "noun", "zh": "员工", "note": "复数 employees", "phonetic": ".emplɒi'i:", "en": "a worker who is hired to perform a job"}, {"word": "camera", "pos": "noun", "zh": "摄像头；相机", "note": "", "phonetic": "'kæmәrә", "en": "equipment for taking photographs (usually consisting of a lightproof box with a lens at one end and light-sensitive…"}, {"word": "license plate", "pos": "noun", "zh": "车牌", "note": "美式拼写；英式为 number plate", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "privacy", "pos": "noun", "zh": "隐私", "note": "", "phonetic": "'praivәsi", "en": "the quality of being secluded from the presence or view of others"}, {"word": "poll", "pos": "noun", "zh": "民意调查", "note": "", "phonetic": "pәul", "en": "an inquiry into public opinion conducted by interviewing a random sample of people"}, {"word": "ban", "pos": "verb", "zh": "禁止", "note": "ban something from somewhere", "phonetic": "bæn", "en": "100 bani equal 1 leu in Moldova"}, {"word": "lawsuit", "pos": "noun", "zh": "诉讼", "note": "face a lawsuit 面临诉讼", "phonetic": "'lɒ:sju:t", "en": "a comprehensive term for any proceeding in a court of law whereby an individual seeks a legal remedy"}], "title_original": "AI surveillance startup Flock to cut several hundred jobs amid backlash, sources say", "summary_original": "Company, which grown rapidly in recent years, has been under scrutiny as privacy concerns grow\nFlock Safety plans to shed about 18% of its employees, people with direct ⁠knowledge of the plans said on Thursday, as the maker of\nAI\n-powered\nsurveillance\ncameras and license-plate readers faces\nmounting opposition\nto its products from communities and ⁠lawmakers.\nThe people said the job ⁠cuts came after ​a voluntary buyout program and were expected to affect roughly 270 employees at Flock, a surveillance technology startup that has seen rapid growth in recent ⁠years. Employees will leave the company at the end of the month.\nContinue reading...", "body_original": "AI surveillance startup Flock to cut several hundred jobs amid backlash, sources say\nCompany, which grown rapidly in recent years, has been under scrutiny as privacy concerns grow\nFlock Safety plans to shed about 18% of its employees, people with direct ⁠knowledge of the plans said on Thursday, as the maker of\nAI\n-powered\nsurveillance\ncameras and license-plate readers faces\nmounting opposition\nto its products from communities and ⁠lawmakers.\nThe people said the job ⁠cuts came after ​a voluntary buyout program and were expected to affect roughly 270 employees at Flock, a surveillance technology startup that has seen rapid growth in recent ⁠years. Employees will leave the company at the end of the month.\nSources declined to be identified as the company has yet to make the plan public.\nFlock declined ⁠to comment.\nIn September, Flock announced a voluntary separation program, asking employees to apply if they wanted to ​leave the company, as Wired reported. The ‌company has about 1,500 employees.\nFlock faces ‌\ngrowing scrutiny\nfrom regulators, lawmakers and privacy advocates, despite drawing strong investor interest among venture capitalists. A ‌recent Reuters/Ipsos poll showed Americans are divided on whether Flock cameras are a good idea. About 38% of the country supports the use of Flock cameras in their community, compared with 47% who oppose their use.\nAcross 49 states, Flock’s network of about 120,000 AI-powered cameras, affixed to streets and highways, automatically read license plates and record vehicles as they pass.\nThe company, based in Atlanta and founded in ‌2017, has raised more than $950m from venture capital investors, with its latest $275m round in March led by Andreessen Horowitz valuing the company at $7.5bn. The funds have supported a ​new US manufacturing facility and an upcoming push into drone products, according to the company.\nFlock provides cameras and software to more than 4,800 law enforcement agencies and nearly 1,000 businesses. The company says its technology helps investigate and solve crimes, but it has come under increasing scrutiny over alleged privacy violations and data-sharing practices.\nPublic backlash ⁠has grown. In September, Florida banned automated license plate readers from state highways, ​citing privacy risks tied to Flock’s ​cameras.\nHome Depot investors recently demanded reviews ​of the retailer’s partnerships with surveillance technology vendors after reports that Flock’s data was used ​in immigration enforcement.\nFlock also ‌faces legal challenges, such ​as a privacy ​lawsuit in Virginia alleging that the widespread deployment of its AI-powered cameras constitutes warrantless surveillance.\nTogether with AI datacenters, Flock cameras have emerged as a flashpoint ahead of November’s midterm elections, with candidates increasingly attacking their opponents by tying them to the technology.\nExplore more on these topics\nSurveillance\nAI (artificial intelligence)\nnews\nShare\nReuse this content", "fetched_at": "2026-10-10T20:57:32.679444", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "Flock", "s": 0.1, "e": 0.488, "sm": 100, "em": 487, "cs": 0, "ce": 5, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "Safety", "s": 0.5, "e"